WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.339
Machine learning has revolutionized a lot of industries today. It can help us

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:11.040
recognize objects  , rank things, even understand what you are saying. But it is

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.660
still in its early stage and faces a lot of challenges. Here I will list three

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.160
major challenges in machine learning nowadays from research to industry and tell you what

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.740
is our current solution to each of them.  The first one is the lack of training data.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:30.990
Data is at the core of any Machine Learning project. However, it is usually

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:35.309
very hard and expensive to obtain labeled data. How to train a model without

00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:40.350
large amount of data is very hot topic today. Transfer learning is one of the

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:45.600
methods to solve this problem. It enables the model to utilize knowledge from

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.660
previously learned tasks and applies them to the new related ones.  For example, in

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:56.579
the image classification  task, very few people will train an entire

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:00.870
convolutional neural network from scratch, which usually needs millions of

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:06.630
labelled images. Instead it is common to use the pre-trained models and fine-tuning

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:11.369
them on the target domain. 
Self-supervised representation

00:01:11.369 --> 00:01:16.200
learning is another way to solve the lack of data problem. It opens up a huge

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:21.450
opportunity for better utilizing large amount of unlabelled data.  Here is a very

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:26.159
famous example in language modeling.
If there is a sentence, but there are some

00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:29.700
missing words in it. How can you fill in those missing words.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.650
Well, the idea is to predict the missing words by learning from the past and

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:39.000
future knowledge. The representation of the language is also learned during

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.710
this process. Google have used this technique to understand searches better

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:48.299
than ever before, which brings one of the biggest leaps forward in the history of

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:52.500
search. The second challenge is that there are usually some discrepancies

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.729
between your training data and production data. Sometimes the model

00:01:56.729 --> 00:02:00.240
works well in your prototyping environment, but fails to generalize in

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:05.280
the real world cases.  Let’s see a few examples here. The model may work well

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.420
in one country but fail in another due to geographical

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:15.750
differences. The model may work in winter but fail in summer due to seasonal differences.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:20.790
The model may work well on mobile but fail on desktop due to user behaviour differences

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.350
So when you are developing your model. You need to be

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:29.250
very careful when you collect your training data. To make it as close to

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:34.760
your target domain as possible. And keep updating your model once it is outdated.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:40.530
The last but not the least challenge is about model scalability. It is a big

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:46.019
issue for a lot of projects in industry. As a machine learning scientist, you need to make

00:02:46.019 --> 00:02:50.640
sure that the model can run fast enough and the model size is small enough, which

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:55.560
is usually a big challenge for a lot of tasks. One of the possible solutions is to

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:00.209
use Post-training quantization. It is a conversion technique that can reduce

00:03:00.209 --> 00:03:05.819
model size. At the same time, it can also improve CPU and hardware accelerator

00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:11.190
latency, with little degradation in model accuracy. Thanks for watching, don't

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:16.160
forget to ring the notification bell and
subscribe us.

